From ac0bec0dbc142339498c202cedee3cf03ffd91ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guy Lyons <guylyons2@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 08:57:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] macos-arm64: reflections only on glossy surfaces;
 reflection history clipping; rt_shadows 2

Source puts an environment map on nearly every lightmapped material as a
cheap specular term; tracing a real reflection onto concrete and plaster
read as a milky haze over the whole scene. Reflections are now limited to
glossy surface properties (metal, glass, tile, ...) with per-property
roughness. The reflection history is clipped against the current frame's
neighbourhood so a reflected object that moved does not trail. rt_shadows 2
darkens with shadows from all geometry, sharpening the baked shadows'
edges (costly: about double the trace).
---
 game/client/rt_layer.cpp | 49 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 rtmetal/rtmetal.mm       | 21 ++++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 58 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/game/client/rt_layer.cpp b/game/client/rt_layer.cpp
index e9f6ad1..0d0cb25 100644
